cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you replicate, build on, or benchmark against this repository
  (the capacity meter, the deterministic integer training battery,
  the gate protocols, or any booked result), cite it as below AND
  pin the exact commit: every citation must name the git commit
  sha (and tag, if any) it relies on — the lab is a moving ledger
  and results are amended in place by dated entries, so an
  unpinned citation is unverifiable. The verdict-by-verdict ledger
  (docs/RESULTS.md) is the citable record; name the specific
  verdict entry plus the commit sha that contains it.
title: "llmopt: an oracle-verified LLM inference and training optimization lab"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "39hops"
repository-code: "https://github.com/39hops/llmopt"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - LLM inference optimization
  - deterministic training
  - integer-exact neural networks
  - verified search
  - reproducibility
